  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Manoj Tuljaram Talbhandare And Anr vs The State Of Maharashtra on 23 August, 2023 Author: N. J. Jamadar Bench: N. J. Jamadar 29-ABA2373-2023.DOC Santos IN THE HIGH COURT OF JUDICATURE AT BOMBAY CRIMINAL APPELLATE JURISDICTION ANTICIPATORY BAIL APPLICATION NO. 2373 OF 2023 Manoj Tuljaram Talbhandare and anr. ...Applicants Versus State of Maharashtra ... Respondent Mr. Ritesh Thobde, for the Applicant. Mr. N. B. Patil, APP for the State. CORAM: N. J. JAMADAR, J. DATED : 23rd AUGUST, 2023 PC:- 2. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with CR No.314 of 2023 registered with Faujdar Chawadi Police Station for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 188, 272 and 273 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 (\"the Penal Code\") and Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(ii), 26(2)(iv) read with Section 27(3) (E), 30(2)(A), 59 of The Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006.",
    "facts": "2. This is an application for pre-arrest bail in connection with CR No.314 of 2023 registered with Faujdar Chawadi Police Station for the offences punishable under Sections 328, 188, 272 and 273 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860 (\"the Penal Code\") and Sections 26(2)(i), 26(2)(ii), 26(2)(iv) read with Section 27(3) (E), 30(2)(A), 59 of The Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3. Pursuant to information, the Food Safety Officer accompanied by the police personnel conducted a raid at the godown of one Mallinath Katare. Accused No.1 Ganesh Katare was found therein in possession of the contraband articles 29-ABA2373-2023.DOC worth Rs.4,88,037/-. It transpired that the said contraband articles were supplied by the applicant. 4. The learned Counsel for the applicant submitted that there is no material to establish the nexus between the applicant and contraband articles. It is recorded in the earlier order that when raid was conducted at the godown, accused No.1 - Manoj Tuljaram Talbhandare And Anr vs The State Of Maharashtra on 28 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/109266908/ 1 Ganesh Tajanji Katare was found in possession of the contraband articles being Gutakha and Pan Masala, who named the Applicants. Learned APP, on telephonic instructions of the Investigating Officer of the concerned police station, submits that investigation is complete and charge-sheet is already filed and the case is registered as Sessions Case No.205 of 2024 in concerned Court.",
